{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n`origin/main` is currently RED on the CI **Module-size gate**: `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` is **803 LOC**, exceeding the absolute 800-LOC hard cap (`.github/module-size-limit.txt`). The gate (`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`, step \"Module-size gate\") runs `find src/rebar -name '*.py' | xargs wc -l` over the WHOLE tree with no allowlist, so this reddens EVERY open Gerrit change with `Verified -1` — no change (1377/e34a, 1379/bdb8, and any future) can reach `Verified +1` until the file is back under the cap.\n\nEvidence:\n- `git show origin/main:src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py | wc -l` -> 803 (cap 800; only file over cap on origin/main).\n- Change 1377 (story e34a) got `Verified -1` solely on this gate; the file is unmodified by that change.\n- The file crossed the cap around commit 339262b990 (\"af11: silence unrelated ambiguity in close scan\").\n\n## Approach — split along the existing completion-precheck call-graph seam\nExtract the self-contained **completion-verification precheck** cluster out of `transition_close.py` into a new sibling module `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close_precheck.py`. These four functions form a closed sub-graph — only `_completion_precheck` is called by `close_ticket`; the other three are private helpers reachable ONLY through it:\n- `_completion_precheck` (the pre-close, outside-the-lock verification half; called by `close_ticket`)\n- `_has_live_replacement_link` (called only by `_completion_precheck`)\n- `_is_live_ticket` (called only by `_has_live_replacement_link`)\n- `_referencing_commit_exists` (called only by `_completion_precheck`)\n\nThe module-level constant `_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES` (used ONLY by `_has_live_replacement_link`) moves with the cluster. `_PLAN_REVIEW_CLOSE_TYPES` and `_raise_plan_review_close_gate_error` and `_compact_on_close` STAY in `transition_close.py` (they are called by `close_ticket`, not by the precheck). This is a genuine call-graph seam (not a mechanical trim): the cluster is the \"verify\" phase of the load-bearing verify->close->sign order documented in the module docstring.\n\nPost-split sizes: `transition_close.py` ~= 480 LOC (in the 200-500 target band); new `transition_close_precheck.py` ~= 340 LOC (in band, > 100-LOC floor). No file left over 800; no file created under 100.\n\n### Consumers of the moved symbols (enumerated — the only edges that must be rewired)\n- `close_ticket` (same file) calls `_completion_precheck(...)` at ~line 638 -> after the split it imports it from `transition_close_precheck`.\n- `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` imports `_referencing_commit_exists` (line 24) and calls it directly (no monkeypatch) -> update its import path + the docstring path reference (line 4) to `transition_close_precheck`. This is an import-path update only; the assertions are unchanged.\n- Interface tests (`test_completion_gate.py`, `test_close_gate_subtree.py`) mention `_completion_precheck` ONLY in docstrings and drive it through `transition` — no code import to change (docstring path may be updated for accuracy, optional).\n- No other `src/` module imports any of the four moved symbols (verified via grep: the only cross-module imports from `transition_close` are `close_ticket`, `sign_completion_verdict`, `_verdict_manifest`, `_material_drifted`, none of which move).\n\n## Test strategy (held-out, behavior-preserving)\nThis is a pure move (no logic change), so the guard is characterization + the existing suite:\n1. Keep `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` green after repointing its import (its `_referencing_commit_exists` assertions exercise the moved function in its new home).\n2. Run the full lifecycle/close interface suites unchanged (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py`, `test_close_gate_subtree.py`, `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py`, `test_attestation_signing.py`, `test_llm_disposition_plumbing.py`) — all must pass with zero edits to their assertions, proving no behavioral regression.\n3. Add a small import-surface test asserting `transition_close_precheck` exposes `_completion_precheck`/`_referencing_commit_exists` and that `transition_close.close_ticket` still resolves the precheck (guards against a future re-break of the seam).\n4. `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean; the module-size gate (`tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` mirror) green.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` is <= 800 LOC (target 200-500), split ONLY along the completion-precheck call-graph seam above — not a mechanical trim, and no new file < 100 LOC.\n- [ ] New module `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close_precheck.py` holds the four precheck functions + `_NON_COMPLETION_BUG_CLASSES`, and is itself within the 100-800 LOC policy band.\n- [ ] The CI Module-size gate passes (no `src/rebar/**/*.py` over 800), restoring reachable `Verified +1` on Gerrit changes.\n- [ ] Existing close/completion tests pass with no assertion changes (behavior unchanged); `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` import path repointed to the new module.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785866224192823001,"uuid":"a1a2468f-fec4-4aac-8ebc-c6ca93f4aaca"}